  {
    "id": "request-lifecycle",
    "caption": "One request's journey: queue wait and the compute-bound prefill make up time to first token; the memory-bound decode loop sets streaming speed.",
    "alt": "A client sends a request. The server tokenizes it on the CPU and places it in a waiting queue. The scheduler admits it when KV-cache space is free. Prefill processes the whole prompt in one pass, writes the KV cache and produces the first token. The decode loop then produces one token per step, reading and appending to the KV cache, and streams each token back to the client until a stop condition.",
